{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/pulls/24","id":4861440276,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU7dI888AAAABIcOxFA","html_url":"https://github.com/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/pull/24","diff_url":"https://github.com/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/pull/24.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/pull/24.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/issues/24","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/pulls/24/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/pulls/24/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/issues/24/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/statuses/5c192f34bad064b14e238747c2c569347257a62c","number":24,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"DeepEye A: 3D control foundations, calibration intake and sensing evidence","user":{"login":"carolwjade","id":328016885,"node_id":"U_kgDOE40j9Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/328016885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carolwjade","html_url":"https://github.com/carolwjade","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carolwjade/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carolwjade/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carolwjade/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carolwjade/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carolwjade/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carolwjade/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carolwjade/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carolwjade/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carolwjade/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"DeepEye needs consistent state across editable 3D geometry, sensor observations, completed AI candidates and final motion commits. This draft adds reviewed editor/control foundations, PC_DIRECT lifecycle and stop handling, bounded pipe framing, offline calibration intake and sensing experiments.\n\nThe latest change archives one coupled finite-element solve and its independent saved-output review. GMRES strictly converged (info0, 47 callbacks, residual 1.526e-18), but receiver errors **5.8587% / 3.5278% exceed the unchanged 1% gates**. The original failed result remains; no qualified sensing model is installed. New Schur-sign and sparse-archive corrections retain their failing controls and exact source snapshots.\n\nValidation and evidence:\n\n- [298-member coupled-solve archive](https://github.com/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/blob/66913fa61270b4e61d453c245d927824548bc267/competition/deepeye/evidence/system/a-coupled-solve-20261023/README.md): one actual solve (70.984s / 3.435GB), raw outputs, source pins, independent audit and root decision. The audit independently checks saved updates, residual/receiver arithmetic and selected equations; full augmented row norm and full direct/reduced boolean retain producer provenance. ZIP members, committed blobs and remote head verified.\n- [Coupled assembly](https://github.com/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/blob/105696bd61e2263bee133525dca87f7d8c18aa45/competition/deepeye/evidence/system/a-coupled-face-closure-20261023/README.md) and [Gauss8 source consistency](https://github.com/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/blob/490adb3bc7a1190b8f2cf424d29f5c987ec63b42/competition/deepeye/evidence/system/a-source8-enrichment-20261023/README.md) retain independently reviewed source/assembly results and earlier failed accuracy screens.\n- [R02 calibration intake](https://github.com/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/blob/b8bc4516ee05cfc2a50714498e0456e936b8ec3a/competition/deepeye/evidence/system/a-r02-calibration-ingest-20261022/README.md): 11 new groups and independent review; four channels with eight distinct reference levels, bounded input, explicit ADC decoding and exclusive outputs. No physical calibration is inferred.\n- [Software checkpoint](https://github.com/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/blob/0b30bab0253f655506682c95e3e9d67ae4234565/competition/deepeye/evidence/system/a-background-checkpoint-20261021/README.md), [stateful control adoption](https://github.com/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/blob/68814fc6963f8ad8e774aa25f598bbd94c34acc1/competition/deepeye/docs/stateful_owner_adoption.md) and [pipe framing](https://github.com/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/blob/22adf16db68b390d38e5718af2dac040cbb05f74/competition/deepeye/docs/actor_ipc_framing.md) are reused. No old project tests or baseline board experiments were repeated for this increment.\n- [Hardware preparation](https://github.com/carolwjade/CarlandFPGA/blob/1be741a896e28eb38d42bbea80dce125755dba02/competition/deepeye/evidence/system/a-r02-hardware-docs-completeness-20261021/README.md): 17-item BOM and wiring documentation. The previous 384/384 base-overlay result is a historical baseline; custom DeepEye bit/HWH and integrated board/simulator evidence remain pending.\n\nNext integration target is a new real-PL observation driving a headless PC_DIRECT physical step and expiry stop, using a clearly labelled digital fixture where needed. Full ADC sensing, actual project inference, three physical capture paths for HIL, native 3D/UI, both H12 routes and formal R03/all29 acceptance remain open. Concurrent exclusive Save As also remains open.\n\nH01-H15 remain mandatory under `DEEPEYE-HUMAN-LOCK-20261014/revision1`, requirements SHA256 `c229834bfc2292f5fe4411fc9f12c68487008f9d1adaf31f0144ee7a98173804`.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-14T17:00:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T04:32:56Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"00949a2f6e00604921878aca22bc04c89bf841fc","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"carolw